---
title: Sharing your mod
sidebar:
  order: 16
---

You share a mod as a **patch**: a file that holds only the differences between your mod and the original game. Players apply it to their own copy of Paper Mario, so you share your work without sharing the game itself.

## Exporting a patch

{% steps %}
1. Select **Mod > Export Patch...**.
2. Choose where to save the patch. It's named after your mod's folder, such as `my-mod.bps`.
3. Select **Export**.
{% /steps %}

## Publishing on Star Haven

[Star Haven](https://starhaven.dev) hosts mods for players to find and download. To publish yours, sign in to Star Haven and open [Share a mod](https://starhaven.dev/create). Fill in the title, the game, and a short description, select **Upload…** and choose your `.bps` patch, then select **Publish**.

## Sending the patch to players

You can also send players the `.bps` file yourself. To play it, they apply it to a Paper Mario (US) ROM in `.z64` format, then load the patched ROM in an emulator or on a flashcart. [Playing mods](/play) walks them through it.
